    /// en: "Every wake is encrypted to a key pair that never leaves this phone (Web Push, RFC 8291), so nobody who learns your endpoint can forge a new alert — though your push server could replay one you already received, Rún limits how often a repeat can trigger the banner — and every wake is the same fixed size. Your messages wait encrypted on the relay until you open Rún, which fetches them over Tor and decrypts them locally with the key derived from your PIN or passphrase."
